<title>USA: Tandy cites tough retail market for lower earnings.</title>
<headline>Tandy cites tough retail market for lower earnings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tandy Corp on Thursday cited a difficult consumer electronics retail market for its lower third quarter earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;The results announced today reflect a tough consumer electronics retail environment that the industry has been experiencing,&quot; John V. Roach, Tandy chairman and chief executive officer said in a statement.</p>
<p>This morning, Tandy reported third quarter earnings at $0.35 per share versus $0.66 last year.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
